//! Replays Go's records and exports, generated by the oracle (see each
//! file's header), so the comparisons of `tests/oracle.rs` also run where
//! no Go toolchain is available. No expected value in them was written by
//! hand.
//!
//! - `tests/data/addrmgr_opvectors.txt`: the hand-written scripts, with
//!   Go's final exports kept whole in `tests/data/opvectors/<name>.pe` and
//!   its export at each `rt.checkpoint` in
//!   `tests/data/opvectors/<name>.<checkpoint>.pe`, each pinned by the
//!   digests of its checkpoint record.
//! - `tests/data/addrmgr_genvectors.txt`: a fixed set of generated scripts
//!   (`tests/support/generator.rs` from a fixed seed, every network and
//!   both coin types), each kept with Go's records and the digest of what
//!   the export comparison compares (`covered_digest`), so a replay
//!   compares the same thing without a 15 KB file per script.
//! - `tests/data/addrmgr_wovectors.txt`: the same for a fixed set of
//!   generated watching-only scripts (`generate_watching_as`: every kind,
//!   created from an account extended public key of either coin type or
//!   converted from a seed's wallet on either coin type, on every network).
//! - `tests/data/addrmgr_passvectors.txt`: the same for a fixed set of
//!   generated passphrase scripts (`generate_passphrase_as`: per-account
//!   passphrases and imported voting accounts on wallets created from a
//!   seed or from an account extended public key, on every network).
//! - `tests/data/addrmgr_changevectors.txt`: the same for a fixed set of
//!   generated passphrase-change scripts (`generate_change_as`: changes of
//!   either passphrase on wallets created from a seed, created from an
//!   account extended public key, or converted, on every network).
//! - `tests/data/txstore_genvectors.txt`: the same for a fixed set of
//!   generated transaction store scripts (`tests/support/txgen.rs`,
//!   `generate_txstore`, on every network, some with the chain sections in
//!   digest mode).
//! - `tests/data/txstore_credit_genvectors.txt`: the same for a fixed set
//!   of generated transaction store scripts that draw the credit slice's
//!   operations too (`generate_txstore_credits`).
//! - `tests/data/txstore_cms_genvectors.txt` and
//!   `tests/data/txstore_select_genvectors.txt`: the same for the
//!   generated scripts that draw the commitment and multisig slice's
//!   operations (`generate_txstore_cms`) and input selection with `Spender`
//!   (`generate_txstore_select`, whose random selections compare exactly,
//!   the bytes drawn included).
//! - `tests/data/aux_genvectors.txt`: the same for a fixed set of generated
//!   auxiliary record scripts (`tests/support/auxgen.rs`, `generate_aux`,
//!   every other one with its operations in groups by `group_aux`).
//! - `tests/data/creation_vectors.txt`: the same for the creation set
//!   (`tests/support/generator.rs`, `creation_set`: same-seed creation of
//!   ADR-0001 section 8 over seed lengths and kinds, public passphrases and
//!   the creation flows, on every network).
//! - `tests/data/ptr_genvectors.txt`: the same for a fixed set of generated
//!   scripts shaped like dcrwallet's `processTransactionRecord`
//!   (`tests/support/ptrgen.rs`, `generate_ptr`: address manager members
//!   in the transaction store's `update` groups).
//!
//! A Go record of kind `Panic` is matched by any Rust error
//! (`check_record`; ADR-0002 section 3, ADR-0012 Rule 2).

#![allow(
    clippy::arithmetic_side_effects,
    reason = "test code: small counts, lengths and generator sizes"
)]

